§ `Section 672.34 -- Verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder`

-- 672.34: where the jury, or the judge or provincial court judge where there is no jury, finds that an accused committed the act or made the omission that formed the basis of the offence charged, but was at the time suffering from mental disorder so as to be
-- exempt from criminal responsibility by virtue of subsection 16(1), the jury or the judge shall render a verdict that the accused committed the act or made the omission but is not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder.
-- fork: F-DUTY-GATE
-- src:13485 | 672.34 Where the jury, or the judge or provincial court judge where there is no jury, finds that an accused committed the act or made the omission that formed the basis of the offence charged, but was at the time suffering from mental disorder so as to be exempt from criminal responsibility by virtue of subsection 16(1), the jury or the judge shall render a verdict that the accused committed the act or made the omission but is not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder.
@ref s 672.34 (src:13485)
GIVEN `the jury, or the judge or provincial court judge where there is no jury, finds that the accused committed the act or made the omission that formed the basis of the offence charged` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the finder finds that the accused was at the time suffering from mental disorder so as to be exempt from criminal responsibility by virtue of subsection 16(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.34 the jury or the judge must render a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder` MEANS
    IF `the jury, or the judge or provincial court judge where there is no jury, finds that the accused committed the act or made the omission that formed the basis of the offence charged` AND `the finder finds that the accused was at the time suffering from mental disorder so as to be exempt from criminal responsibility by virtue of subsection 16(1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the jury, or the judge or provincial court judge where there is no jury, finds that an accused committed the act or made the omission that formed the basis of the offence charged, but was at the time suffering from mental disorder"

§ `Sections 672.35 and 672.36 -- Effect of the verdict`

-- 672.35: where a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder is rendered, the accused shall not be found guilty or convicted of the offence, but ...
-- The chapeau: the section bars a finding of guilt or a conviction of the offence.
-- src:13487 | 672.35 Where a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder is rendered, the accused shall not be found guilty or convicted of the offence, but
@ref s 672.35 (src:13487)
GIVEN `a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder is rendered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.35 the section bars a finding of guilt or a conviction of the offence` MEANS
    IF `a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder is rendered`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder is rendered"

-- 672.35(a): the accused may plead autrefois acquit in respect of any subsequent charge relating to that offence.
-- fork: F-GRANT-WHERE
-- src:13488 | (a) the accused may plead autrefois acquit in respect of any subsequent charge relating to that offence;
@ref s 672.35(a) (src:13488)
GIVEN `a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder is rendered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the subsequent charge relates to that offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.35(a) the accused may plead autrefois acquit in respect of a subsequent charge relating to that offence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder is rendered` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder is rendered"
        IF `the subsequent charge relates to that offence` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in respect of any subsequent charge relating to that offence"

-- 672.35(b): any court may take the verdict into account in considering an application for judicial interim release or in considering what dispositions to make or sentence to impose for any other offence.
-- fork: F-GRANT-WHERE
-- src:13489 | (b) any court may take the verdict into account in considering an application for judicial interim release or in considering what dispositions to make or sentence to impose for any other offence; and
@ref s 672.35(b) (src:13489)
GIVEN `a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder is rendered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is considering an application for judicial interim release` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is considering what dispositions to make or sentence to impose for any other offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.35(b) any court may take the verdict into account` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder is rendered` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder is rendered"
        IF `the court is considering an application for judicial interim release` OR `the court is considering what dispositions to make or sentence to impose for any other offence` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "any court may take the verdict into account in considering an application for judicial interim release or in considering what dispositions to make or sentence to impose for any other offence"

-- 672.35(c): the Parole Board of Canada or any provincial parole board may take the verdict into account in considering an application by the accused for parole or for a record suspension under the Criminal Records Act in respect of any other offence.
-- fork: F-GRANT-WHERE
-- src:13490 | (c) the Parole Board of Canada or any provincial parole board may take the verdict into account in considering an application by the accused for parole or for a record suspension under the Criminal Records Act in respect of any other offence.
@ref s 672.35(c) (src:13490)
GIVEN `a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder is rendered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Parole Board of Canada or a provincial parole board is considering an application by the accused for parole or for a record suspension under the Criminal Records Act in respect of any other offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.35(c) the Parole Board of Canada or a provincial parole board may take the verdict into account` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder is rendered` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder is rendered"
        IF `the Parole Board of Canada or a provincial parole board is considering an application by the accused for parole or for a record suspension under the Criminal Records Act in respect of any other offence` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in considering an application by the accused for parole or for a record suspension under the Criminal Records Act in respect of any other offence"

-- 672.36: a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder is not a previous conviction for the purposes of any offence under any Act of Parliament for which a greater punishment is provided by reason of previous convictions.
-- Asked in the positive: is the verdict a previous conviction for that purpose? The text says no (a flat negative): JUST FALSE.
-- src:13492 | 672.36 A verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder is not a previous conviction for the purposes of any offence under any Act of Parliament for which a greater punishment is provided by reason of previous convictions.
@ref s 672.36 (src:13492)
GIVEN `it is a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence is under an Act of Parliament and a greater punishment is provided for it by reason of previous convictions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.36 the verdict is a previous conviction for the purposes of an offence that carries a greater punishment by reason of previous convictions` MEANS
    IF `it is a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder` AND `the offence is under an Act of Parliament and a greater punishment is provided for it by reason of previous convictions`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is not a previous conviction for the purposes of any offence under any Act of Parliament for which a greater punishment is provided by reason of previous convictions"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for the purposes of any offence under any Act of Parliament for which a greater punishment is provided by reason of previous convictions"

§ `Section 672.37 -- Application for federal employment`

-- 672.37(1): application for federal employment means an application form relating to (a) employment in any department, as defined in section 2 of the Financial Administration Act; (b) employment by any Crown corporation as defined in subsection 83(1) of that Act;
-- (c) enrolment in the Canadian Forces; or (d) employment in connection with the operation of any work, undertaking or business that is within the legislative authority of Parliament.
-- src:13494 | 672.37 (1) In this section, application for federal employment means an application form relating to
-- src:13495 | (a) employment in any department, as defined in section 2 of the Financial Administration Act;
-- src:13496 | (b) employment by any Crown corporation as defined in subsection 83(1) of the Financial Administration Act;
-- src:13497 | (c) enrolment in the Canadian Forces; or
-- src:13498 | (d) employment in connection with the operation of any work, undertaking or business that is within the legislative authority of Parliament.
@ref s 672.37(1); s 672.37(1)"application for federal employment"; s 672.37(1)(a); s 672.37(1)(b); s 672.37(1)(c); s 672.37(1)(d) (src:13494-13498)
GIVEN `it is an application form` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it relates to employment in any department, as defined in section 2 of the Financial Administration Act` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (a)
      `it relates to employment by any Crown corporation as defined in subsection 83(1) of the Financial Administration Act` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)
      `it relates to enrolment in the Canadian Forces` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (c)
      `it relates to employment in connection with the operation of any work, undertaking or business that is within the legislative authority of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (d)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.37(1) application for federal employment` MEANS
    IF `it is an application form` AND (    `it relates to employment in any department, as defined in section 2 of the Financial Administration Act`
                                         OR `it relates to employment by any Crown corporation as defined in subsection 83(1) of the Financial Administration Act`
                                         OR `it relates to enrolment in the Canadian Forces`
                                         OR `it relates to employment in connection with the operation of any work, undertaking or business that is within the legislative authority of Parliament`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "application for federal employment means an application form relating to"

-- 672.37(2): no application for federal employment shall contain any question that requires the applicant to disclose any charge or finding that the applicant committed an offence that resulted in a finding or a verdict of not criminally responsible
-- on account of mental disorder if the applicant was discharged absolutely or is no longer subject to any disposition in respect of that offence.
-- fork: F-BAR-IF
-- src:13500 | (2) No application for federal employment shall contain any question that requires the applicant to disclose any charge or finding that the applicant committed an offence that resulted in a finding or a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder if the applicant was discharged absolutely or is no longer subject to any disposition in respect of that offence.
@ref s 672.37(2) (src:13500)
GIVEN `it is an application for federal employment, by s 672.37(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the question requires the applicant to disclose any charge or finding that the applicant committed an offence that resulted in a finding or a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant was discharged absolutely` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant is no longer subject to any disposition in respect of that offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.37(2) the section bars the application for federal employment from containing the question` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is an application for federal employment, by s 672.37(1)` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "No application for federal employment shall contain"
        IF `it is an application for federal employment, by s 672.37(1)` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): "application for federal employment"
        IF `the question requires the applicant to disclose any charge or finding that the applicant committed an offence that resulted in a finding or a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder` AND (`the applicant was discharged absolutely` OR `the applicant is no longer subject to any disposition in respect of that offence`) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the applicant was discharged absolutely or is no longer subject to any disposition in respect of that offence"

-- 672.37(3): any person who uses or authorizes the use of an application for federal employment that contravenes subsection (2) is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
-- The answer is the class of offence (the penalty itself is in Part XXVII, outside this part): the core `Punishment` carries the mode and "no imprisonment/fine is stated".
-- src:13502 | (3) Any person who uses or authorizes the use of an application for federal employment that contravenes subsection (2) is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 672.37(3) (src:13502)
GIVEN `the person uses or authorizes the use of the application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application contravenes subsection 672.37(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Punishment
`s 672.37(3) the punishment of the person who uses or authorizes the use of a contravening application` MEANS
    IF `the person uses or authorizes the use of the application` AND `the application contravenes subsection 672.37(2)`
    THEN JUST (Punishment OF `on summary conviction`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any person who uses or authorizes the use of an application for federal employment that contravenes subsection (2)"
